Multiplying the numerators and denominators, we get:
\begin{align*}
\frac{12x^4}{14x^3} \cdot \frac{35x}{3x}
\end{align*}
Canceling out the common factors, we have:
\begin{align*}
\frac{12x^4}{14x^3} \cdot \frac{35x}{3x} &= \frac{12x^4 \cdot 35}{14x^3 \cdot 3x} \\
&= \frac{12 \cdot 35 \cdot x^4}{14 \cdot 3 \cdot x^3} \\
&= \frac{12 \cdot 35}{14 \cdot 3} \cdot \frac{x^4}{x^3} \\
&= \frac{980}{99} \cdot \frac{x^4}{x^3} \\
&= \frac{980}{99} \cdot \frac{x^3}{1} \cdot \frac{1}{x} \\
&= \frac{980}{99 \cdot x}
\end{align*}
Therefore, the simplified expression is $\boxed{\frac{980}{99x}}$.

