The sum $11^1 + 11^2 + 11^3 + \ldots + 11^9$ is a geometric series with first term $11$ and common ratio $11$. Using the formula for the sum of a geometric series, we find that the sum is \begin{align*}
\frac{11^{10}-1}{11-1} &= \frac{11^{10}-1}{10} \\
&= \frac{11^9(11^1+11^2+\ldots+11^8)+1}{10} \\
&= \frac{11^9(11^{9}+11^8+11^7+\ldots+11^1)}{10} \\
&= \frac{11^9(11+11^8+11^9+\ldots+11^{25})}{10}
\end{align*}We can see that the tens digit of $11^9$ is $1$, the hundreds digit of $11^9$ is $1$, and the thousands digit of $11^9$ is $1$. Therefore, the sum of the series is \begin{align*}
\frac{11^9(1+11^8+11^9+\ldots+11^{25})}{10} &= \frac{11^9(1+11^8+11^9+\ldots+11^{25})}{10} \\
&= \frac{11^9(1+11^8+11^9+\ldots+11^{25})}{10} \\
&= \frac{11^9(1+11^8+11^9+\ldots+11^{25})}{10} \\
&= \frac{11^9(1+11^8+11^9+\ldots+11^{25})}{10} \\
&= \boxed{2}.
\end{align*}
The answer is: 2

