What is the remainder when $163^3$ is divided by $100$?
Steps: We can simplify $163^3$ by using the fact that $163=13^2$. We have \begin{align*}
163^3&=(13^2)^3\\
&=13^{2\cdot3}^3\\
&=13^6\\
&=13\cdot13\cdot13^2\\
&\equiv13\cdot13\cdot1\pmod{100}\\
&\equiv3\cdot13\cdot1\pmod{100}\\
&\equiv3\cdot13\pmod{100}\\
&\equiv3\pmod{100}.
\end{align*}The remainder when $163^3$ is divided by $100$ is $\boxed{3}$.

