&= \bold{a} \times (5 \bold{a}) - \bold{a} \times (7 \bold{b}) - 3 \bold{b} \times (5 \bold{a}) + 3 \bold{b} \times (7 \bold{b}) \\
&= -5 \bold{a} \times \bold{a} - 7 \bold{a} \times \bold{b} - 3 \bold{b} \times (5 \bold{a}) - 21 \bold{b} \times \bold{b}
\end{align*}We know that $\bold{a} \times \bold{a} = \bold{a} \times \bold{b} = \bold{b} \times \bold{a} = \bold{b} \times \bold{b} = 0$, so the above simplifies to $-21 \bold{b} \times \bold{b}$.  Thus, $k = \boxed{21}$.
The answer is: 21

