\]Now, we can find the cross product of $(5 \bold{a} + 7 \bold{b})$ with $\bold{a}$: \begin{align*}
(5 \bold{a} + 7 \bold{b}) \times \bold{a} &= (5 \bold{a} \times \bold{a}) + (7 \bold{b} \times \bold{a}) \\
&= \bold{0} + (7 \bold{b} \times \bold{a})
\end{align*}Since $\bold{b} \times \bold{a}$ is a vector, we must have $7 \bold{b} \times \bold{a} = \bold{b} \times \bold{a}$, which is true. Therefore, \begin{align*}
