8^3&=8\cdot8\cdot8=\boxed{512}
\end{align*}
Next, we calculate $2^{(3^2)}$:
\begin{align*}
2^{(3^2)}&=2^{9}=2\cdot2\cdot2\cdot2\cdot2\cdot2\cdot2\cdot2\cdot2=\boxed{512}
\end{align*}
Finally, we add up the three results:
\begin{align*}
317^3+8^3-(2^{(3^2})&+317^3) \\
=317^3+512-512+317^3 \\
=2\cdot317^3
\end{align*}
Therefore, $317^{3}+8^{3}-(2^{(3^{2})}+317^{3})=\boxed{2\cdot317^3}$.

