\begin{align*}
\frac{5}{2} &= \frac{x}{34},
\end{align*}
where $x$ is the height of the tree.

Solving for $x$, we get:
\begin{align*}
x &= \frac{5}{2} \cdot 34 \\
x &= \frac{5 \cdot 34}{2} \\
x &= 55
\end{align*}

2. Find the height of the tree.
